&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;A SORCERER LORD!
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;BECAUSE WHY HAVE A SIMPLE GENERAL IF FOR 25 MORE POINTS YOU CAN TURN HIM INTO A POWERFUL WIZARD?!
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Furthermore, it is not only the sorcerer, but I have taken the task of designing a floating magical platform powered by demonic fire to transport the Sorcerer Lord across the battlefield with speed and comfort, from a privileged position to command the armies at his feet.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;In game terms, it is not supposed to be a flying unit, but simply to stand out above the rest so that it is clear who it is.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;I designed the platform from scratch and using some bits taken from here and there. For the Sorcerer Lord I used the &amp;#34;Dwarf Wizard&amp;#34; model created by Tom Wiggins as a base and edited it a little.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;NOTE: Be VERY careful when removing the supports from the Sorcerer Lord, the staff can break easily.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
